#: ../../../../Modules/FindDCMTK.cmake:113
msgid "Example: Finding DCMTK Without This Module"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../Modules/FindDCMTK.cmake:115
msgid ""
"To explicitly use the ``DCMTKConfig.cmake`` package configuration file "
"(recommended when possible) and find DCMTK in *config mode* without using "
"this module, the ``NO_MODULE`` option can be given to :command:"
"`find_package`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../Modules/FindDCMTK.cmake:120
msgid "find_package(DCMTK NO_MODULE)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../Modules/FindDCMTK.cmake:125
msgid "Example: Creating Imported Target"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../Modules/FindDCMTK.cmake:127
msgid ""
"In the following example, DCMTK is searched with this module and an :ref:"
"`imported target <Imported Targets>` is conditionally created to provide "
"DCMTK usage requirements which can be easily linked to project targets.  For "
"example, if DCMTK is found in *config mode*, the ``DCMTK::DCMTK`` imported "
"target will be available through the found config files instead:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../Modules/FindDCMTK.cmake:134
msgid ""
"find_package(DCMTK)\n"
"\n"
"# Upstream DCMTKConfig.cmake already provides DCMTK::DCMTK imported target\n"
"if(DCMTK_FOUND AND NOT TARGET DCMTK::DCMTK)\n"
"  add_library(DCMTK::DCMTK INTERFACE IMPORTED)\n"
"  set_target_properties(\n"
"    DCMTK:DCMTK\n"
"    PROPERTIES\n"
"      INTERFACE_LINK_LIBRARIES \"${DCMTK_LIBRARIES}\"\n"
"      INTERFACE_INCLUDE_DIRECTORIES \"${DCMTK_INCLUDE_DIRS}\"\n"
"  )\n"
"endif()\n"
"\n"
"target_link_libraries(example PRIVATE DCMTK::DCMTK)"
msgstr ""
